---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Terms · canivibecodeit';
const description = 'The short, honest rules for using canivibecodeit.com.';
---

<Base {title} {description}>
  <main class="wrap legal">
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="microlabel">last updated 2026-08-10 · canivibecodeit.com, run by Rob Hallam, sole trader, UK</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Verdicts are opinions.</strong> "YES you can vibecode it" is editorial judgment
        plus community input, not professional advice. Prices and free tiers change; we chase
        them but they can lag. Check before you cancel anything that matters.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The dataset is MIT.</strong> App entries, verdicts, and prompts live in
        a <a href="https://github.com/canivibecodeit/canivibecodeit">public repo</a> under the MIT
        license. Fork it, remix it, ship it. Attribution appreciated, not required.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Prompts are free forever.</strong> No paywall on any verdict or prompt, ever.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Accounts.</strong> Free, used only for saving your stack and digest settings.
        Don't automate abuse against the site (vote flooding, scraping at hostile rates, spam
        submissions); we can remove accounts that do. You can delete your account any time
        on <a href="/account">/account</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sponsorship.</strong> Sponsor slots are paid placements, always labeled, and
        never influence verdicts. The commercial fine print (approval, refunds, scheduling)
        lives on <a href="/sponsor">/sponsor</a> and applies to every purchase there.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No warranty.</strong> The site is provided as-is. If a prompt one-shots your
        replacement, wonderful. If it doesn't, your subscription is still there.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Governing law:</strong> England and Wales. If some of this is ever held
        unenforceable, the rest stands.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="legal-foot">Privacy lives at <a href="/privacy">/privacy</a>.</p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding-top: 48px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 36px);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .legal p,
  .legal li {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .legal ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .legal a {
    color: var(--primary);
  }
  .legal-foot {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
